  "body": "The event loop processing model references 'current high resolution time' multiple times:\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop-processing-model:current-high-resolution-time\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop-processing-model:current-high-resolution-time-2\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop-processing-model:current-high-resolution-time-3\r\n- https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#event-loop-processing-model:current-high-resolution-time-4\r\n\r\nhowever hr-time specifies:\r\n> The current high resolution time given a [global object](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/webappapis.html#global-object) current global must return the result of [relative high resolution time](https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dfn-relative-high-resolution-time) given [unsafe shared current time](https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dfn-unsafe-shared-current-time) and current global.\r\n- https://w3c.github.io/hr-time/#dfn-current-high-resolution-time\r\n\r\nNo such global object is defined for the event loop. Is the intention maybe to use 'coarsened shared current time' or 'unsafe shared current time'?",
